              "date": "2026-07-30T16:37:51Z"
            }
          ],
          "series_items": [],
          "patch_summary": "This patch fixes a bug in Btrfs where fixup workers can still be running when the fs roots are freed during unmount, leading to memory allocation errors and potential crashes. To solve this, the patch adds explicit flushing of the fixup workqueue before unmount, and also denies new fixup queueing during umount. This ensures that all fixup writeback is completed before declaring BTRFS_FS_STATE_NO_DELAYED_IPUT.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-per-reviewer",
